## Description
This is the last batch of fields to move over for the GraphQL restructure [project](https://github.com/codecov/engineering-team/issues/2118).
It takes `testResults`, `testResultsAggregates`, and `flakeAggregates` which are test analytics related concepts and nests them within the new `repository.testAnalytics` type.

Note that at this time, `testResults` is used by a frontend client but `testResultsAggregates` and `flakeAggregates` are not, so proposing to do a breaking change on the latter 2 fields and a multi-step on the 1st field (merge this pr > cutover the frontend client > delete old fields from this repo).

Closes https://github.com/codecov/engineering-team/issues/2287

Tested by confirming the unit tests when moved over pass as expected.
Also tested in staging that the apis return the expected data.
The duplicated behavior will get cleaned up with this [ticket](https://github.com/codecov/engineering-team/issues/2291) after frontend cutover done.

## Summary of Changes

These were the updates to the schema:

BEFORE
```graphql
type Repository {
  name: String!
  <... other stuff>
  ### see below fields that are currently at repository.<field>
  testResults(
    filters: TestResultsFilters
    ordering: TestResultsOrdering
    first: Int
    after: String
    last: Int
    before: String
  ): TestResultConnection! @cost(complexity: 10, multipliers: ["first", "last"])
  testResultsAggregates: TestResultsAggregates
  flakeAggregates: FlakeAggregates
  <... other stuff>
 }

```

AFTER
```graphql
type Repository {
  name: String!
  <... other stuff>
  ### see anything related to testAnalytics is now nested one level
  testAnalytics: TestAnalytics
 }

type TestAnalytics {
  results(
    filters: TestResultsFilters
    ordering: TestResultsOrdering
    first: Int
    after: String
    last: Int
    before: String
  ): TestResultConnection! @cost(complexity: 10, multipliers: ["first", "last"])
  resultsAggregates: TestResultsAggregates
  flakeAggregates: FlakeAggregates
}
```

This is the GraphQL Query
```graphql
query TestAnalytics(
  $owner:String!,
  $repo: String!,

  # results filters
  $filters: TestResultsFilters,
  $orderingDirection: TestResultsOrdering!,
  # $after: String!, # pagination cursor value
) {
  owner(username:$owner) {
    repository(name: $repo) {
      ... on Repository {
        name

        # old
        testResults(
          filters: $filters,
          ordering: $orderingDirection,
          # after: $after,
          first: 15
          # last: 10
          # before: $before
        ) {
          totalCount
          pageInfo {
            hasNextPage
            hasPreviousPage
            startCursor
            endCursor
          }
        }

        testResultsAggregates{
          totalFails
        }
        flakeAggregates{
          flakeCount
        }

        # new
        testAnalytics {
          results(
            filters: $filters,
            ordering: $orderingDirection,
            # after: $after,
            first: 15
            # last: 10
            # before: $before
          ) {
            totalCount
            pageInfo {
              hasNextPage
              hasPreviousPage
              startCursor
              endCursor
            }
          }


          resultsAggregates{
            totalFails
          }
          flakeAggregates{
            flakeCount
          }
        }
      }
      ... on ResolverError {
        message
      }
    }
  }
}

```

